What is CI/CD in DevOps, and why is it important?
✅ Answer:
 CI/CD stands for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment/Delivery.
CI (Continuous Integration) is the practice where developers frequently integrate code into a shared repository, followed by automated builds and tests.
CD (Continuous Delivery/Deployment) ensures that code changes are automatically tested and released to production with minimal manual intervention.
🚀 Why It’s Important:
CI/CD reduces integration issues, making code deployment faster and safer.
It allows for early bug detection, enhances code quality, and ensures faster time-to-market.
In modern DevOps pipelines, CI/CD is the backbone of automation, enabling rapid innovation and robust software delivery.
🔧 Tools commonly used: Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI, AWS CodePipeline
